# Reference data is fetched, never committed. data/fetch.sh brings it in. No exceptions:
# the four small chr21 extracts used to be committed so Fig. S5 built offline, but two
# other figure scripts reach the network anyway, so the exception bought nothing.
# `data/fetch.sh extracts` pulls them from NCBI in a few seconds; the hashes that pin
# them are in data/checksums.sha256.
data/*.fa
data/*.fa.gz
data/*.fasta
data/*.fasta.gz
data/*.bed
data/*.bb
data/*.bw
data/*.fastq
data/*.fastq.gz
data/*.part
!data/checksums.sha256

# Alignments and signal tracks: large, and derived from the fetched reads.
*.bam
*.bam.bai
*.cram
*.bigWig

# Third-party publications are NOT redistributable. Path-independent on purpose:
# an earlier directory reorganisation silently un-ignored 225 MB of this material.
Gao2026.pdf
**/Gao2026.pdf
GaoSupplementaryMaterials/
**/GaoSupplementaryMaterials/
*.pdf

# Environments and build noise
venv/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.DS_Store
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Scripts write run logs and intermediate panels as a by-product. Those are outputs,
# not deposited data, so a clone that runs `make figures` should not report them as
# untracked. The 16 published figures are all named fig*.png and stay tracked.
results/*_log.txt
results/figures/*.png
!results/figures/fig*.png

# Scratch space for the large intermediates: the genome atlas, the RepeatMasker bed,
# the sequence caches. Repo-relative so nothing is lost to a /tmp clear. Move it with
# GC_WORK, or point at a single file with GC_ATLAS, GC_REPEATMASKER, CHM13_FA, SEQ_CACHE.
work/
